\tr{\td{Mathlib}\td{574,100,326}\td{566,249,736}\td{-7,850,590 (-1.37 \%)}\td{4}\td{120, 128}\td{60, 5,277,996 steps; 64, 5,293,756 steps}}
}

\table{
\tr{\th{Unit (cslib / Mathlib)}\th{ticks and outcome, base}\th{2^17}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Batteries.Data.Char.Basic: Char.all._proof_1~} (96,222 / 321,319)}\td{980,211 / 980,179, accept}\td{136,766 / 136,734, decline}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Char.any._proof_1~} (219,779 / 362,538)}\td{982,310 / 982,260, accept}\td{140,768 / 140,718, decline}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Char.of_any_eq_false_aux._proof_1_15~} (219,799 / 362,559)}\td{3,212,971 / 3,212,970, accept}\td{131,472 / 131,472, decline}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Char.of_any_eq_false_aux._proof_1_18~} (219,801 / 362,561)}\td{3,218,191 / 3,218,190, accept}\td{134,086 / 134,085, decline}}
\tr{\td{con-leche: \code{ConLeche.lpOfData_pack} (13,027)}\td{4,196,461, decline}\td{133,229, decline}}
}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Init, Std, cedar, reachability, navier-stokes-euler: nothing changes.} Every count is identical; the one key that differs is the setting itself, \code{machine.eager.probeBudget}; no unit differs in ticks or outcome.}
\li{\strong{cslib and Mathlib: exactly the four units of the table.} They go from accepted by the machine to declined by it and decided by the reference engine: the machine's accepted units fall by 4, its declines rise by 8 (the warm attempt and the driver's cold retry, which is answered at once), \code{machine.eager.probeCuts} and \code{machine.eager.declined.probe} go from 0 to 4, \code{machine.eager.kept} falls by 4, the reference engine decides 4 more units in 15,760 more steps. The four units take 8.39 M ticks in the base and 0.54 M with the budget: -7.85 M ticks, 3.64 \% of cslib's and 1.37 \% of Mathlib's. The ticks and the outcome of each of the other 397,604 and 714,708 units of the trace are identical, although the sessions are warm: a session is forgotten after such a unit either way. The other counters that differ (calls, records, run words, memo hits, frames) are those of the work inside the four units.}
\li{\strong{con-leche: one unit}, the one that was cut and declined before: its probe is cut at 2^17 instead of 2^22, -4,063,232 ticks (5.74 \% of the corpus's), the same declines, the same units for the reference engine.}
}
}

