\tr{\td{Init}\td{468 (466, 465, 472, 469)}\td{470 (472, 468, 467, 475)}\td{1.005}\td{173, 176}}
\tr{\td{Std}\td{822 (822, 818, 830, 820)}\td{825 (838, 823, 823, 827)}\td{1.005}\td{301, 303}}
\tr{\td{cslib}\td{3,867 (3,867, 3,866, 3,936, 3,843)}\td{3,890 (3,876, 3,895, 3,886, 3,894)}\td{1.006}\td{1,163, 1,170}}
\tr{\td{Mathlib}\td{9,543 (9,621, 9,607, 9,478, 9,462)}\td{9,623 (9,552, 9,694, 9,701, 9,540)}\td{1.008}\td{2,769, 2,876}}
}

\p{So the loader pays 2 to 80 ms per load for the table, half a percent to 0.8 \% of the load, with rounds that overlap on Mathlib; the six ints per declaration and the growth of the arrays show as 3 to 107 MiB of peak resident set in a load alone, and as nothing that the peak of a whole pass shows on any corpus but Mathlib (4,384 and 4,490 MiB in the executable). On the corpora whose pass follows the loader thread (Init, Std, cedar, cslib) that cost is on the critical path, and the pass still gets shorter: the workers' saving is larger than the loader's price there too.}
}

\subtree{
\title{3.9 What the design notes must say}

\ul{
\li{[The driver](design-driver): a paragraph on repeats under "Threads and frontiers" or the scheduler: what a repeat is, that it is admitted and not checked when its original is ACCEPTED, the wait, the setting, that the reference engine as primary engine never skips. Its invariant "the verdict and the deciding unit do not depend on the worker count" holds with the skip, for the reason of section 3.4.}
\li{[The verdict protocol](design-verdict-protocol), "The re-check protocol": "an accept of the primary engine is final" gets its second case, the accept of a repeat on the word of its original.}
\li{[The export loader](design-export-loader): the table of declarations by record ids and the one call that reports a repeat; the store digest is unchanged apart from the new column.}
\li{[The divergence classes](design-official-divergence): the file of section 3.5 is an example of class (d) that exists only with the skip.}
}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{4. The patches, and what an integrator must know}

\p{Four unified diffs against the main tree (paths from the repository root; each was applied to the main tree of this report's end in a dry run). They are kept with the package's working files and handed to the integrator; this report names what they touch.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Patch}\th{Files}\th{Change}}
\tr{\td{1, change 1}\td{\src{rlvm-machine/src/main/java/rlvm/machine/MachineEngine.java}, \src{rlvm-machine/src/test/java/rlvm/machine/M6FacadeTest.java}}\td{\code{DEFAULT_EAGER_PROBE} = 2^17 with its comment; the test asserts the value and that it lies between 63,654 and 458,881}}
\tr{\td{2, change 2, store}\td{\src{rlvm-store/src/main/java/rlvm/store/DeclTable.java}, \src{rlvm-store/src/main/java/rlvm/store/StoreBuilder.java}, \src{rlvm-store/src/test/java/rlvm/store/DeclStoreTest.java}, \src{rlvm-store/README.md}}\td{the column \code{DeclTable.repeatOf} and its writer \code{StoreBuilder.repeatOf}; one test; one README entry}}
\tr{\td{3, change 2, loader}\td{\src{rlvm-load/src/main/java/rlvm/load/Loader.java} (the method \code{declare}, one field, one line of the report), \code{rlvm-load/src/main/java/rlvm/load/Repeats.java} (new), \src{rlvm-load/src/main/java/rlvm/load/LoadTarget.java}, \src{rlvm-load/src/main/java/rlvm/load/StoreTarget.java}, \src{rlvm-load/src/main/java/rlvm/load/LoadReport.java}, \src{rlvm-load/README.md}; tests: \code{RepeatsTest.java} (new), \code{StoreIntegrationTest.java}, \code{Oracle.java}, \code{StoreOracle.java}, \code{FakeTarget.java}, \code{RecordingTarget.java}}\td{the table of declarations by their record ids, the call \code{LoadTarget.repeatOf} (a default method that does nothing), the statistic; the loader's oracle now finds the repeats of every file it loads again from the reference records and compares}}
\tr{\td{4, change 2, driver}\td{\src{rlvm-driver/src/main/java/rlvm/driver/Worker.java}, \src{rlvm-driver/src/main/java/rlvm/driver/RunHost.java}, \src{rlvm-driver/src/main/java/rlvm/driver/StoreHost.java}, \src{rlvm-driver/src/main/java/rlvm/driver/RunConfig.java}, \src{rlvm-driver/src/main/java/rlvm/driver/Run.java}, \src{rlvm-driver/README.md}; tests: \code{RepeatSkipTest.java} (new), \code{Fakes.java}}\td{the skip, the wait of section 3.4, \code{RunHost.unitRepeatOf} (a default method: no unit repeats another), the setting \code{repeats}, two statistics; nine tests}}
}

\ul{
\li{Patch 1 stands alone. Patches 2, 3 and 4 belong together and are published in that order: store, loader, driver. Nothing of \code{rlvm-admit}, \code{rlvm-machine}, \code{rlvm-main} or a build script changes for change 2, and no method named by the machine's force-inline list is renamed, split or removed.}
\li{Change 1 and the work of other packages on \code{rlvm-machine}: the patch touches one constant and one assertion. A change of the machine that moves the tick count of a probe moves nothing here as long as the largest probe that completes stays below 2^17 (it is at 63,654); the statistics of any run say so.}
\li{Change 2 and the work of another package on the loader: in \code{Loader.java} the patch reads the result of \code{out.beginUnit}, adds one call before the segment is written and one after \code{out.complete}. The call must stay in front of everything that moves \code{segBase}, because it compares the two root ordinals with it.}
\li{The code cites this report by its address (\code{RunConfig.skipRepeats}, \code{MachineEngine.DEFAULT_EAGER_PROBE} and the three READMEs), so the address is permanent.}
\li{A changelog entry per change and the revision of the design notes named in sections 2.6 and 3.9 are the integrator's, with the commit.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{5. What was not measured}

\ul{
\li{An idle host: the windows of the guard ran with a load average of 4 to 10 on the other twelve cores, the first windows with 45 to 95.}
\li{The two changes together, in time, in the counters and in the gates: each was built, gated and timed alone against the base. Their effects are on different units (the five units of change 1 are not repeats), so the counters should add.}
\li{The executables with the level fix: the builds that carry it are jars (section 1.1).}
\li{One worker as a timing; x86-64, the architecture of the arena runner; the optional profile-guided build.}
\li{The three budgets 2^16, 2^17 and 2^18 against each other on a calm host: they were timed only in the loaded windows, where they cannot be told apart.}
\li{A budget in the lower gap of the probe sizes (between 1,600 and 34,096 ticks), which would also send six units to the reference engine.}
\li{What the wait of section 3.4 costs when it occurs: it did not occur on any corpus.}
\li{The loader's table on a file with more declarations than Mathlib's 722,000.}
\li{Whether a key without the reducibility hint would find more than the 23, 5 and 21 units it separates on Mathlib, navier-stokes-euler and cslib, and a skip for axioms (four per corpus, a handful of ticks each).}
\li{"Nothing kept between declarations" on navier-stokes-euler, cslib and Mathlib (section 3.7): the exact identity of the other units was shown on the five smaller corpora.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{6. Tools}

\p{All outside the repository. A private build of \code{rlvm-machine} that prints one line per probe with its own ticks (the ticks of the speculative segment, so nested probes are seen separately) and a summary by size; a runner of one-worker count passes with the statistics file and the unit trace, and a comparison of two such runs key by key and unit by unit; the guard runner (one window per launcher, the variants interleaved, a variant may carry settings of its own so that one executable is measured against itself) and its table; a generator of hostile exports on the prelude of the machine's suite (41 files) and a transformation that appends, to every row of that suite, its last declaration once more under a new name, as the same record and as a record of another kind; the official-verdict script (leanchecker in the arena image, no network) and the manifest that \src{scripts/gate-hostile.py} judges.}
}

\p{Findings: [the probes of eager reduction come in three sizes](ins-N4ES), [a declaration that repeats an accepted one needs no second check for the official checker, and the machine's answer for the copy can differ](ins-FS8W).}
